10.1037/pspp0000104,9c0e3d488066f983,1,,"The religion paradox: If religion makes people happy, why are so many dropping out?","Diener, E., Tay, L., & Myers, D. G.",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,"{""target_index"": 1, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""obvious"", ""verdict"": ""undeterminable"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""Yet, this study differed from previous research in three important ways. First, previous research operationalized psychological adjustment as life satisfaction (Stavrova et al., 2013), subjective well-being (Diener et al., 2011), depression (Leurent et al., 2013), or social self-esteem (Gebauer et al., 2012b). From an RASV perspective, however, global self-esteem is the most appropriate adjustment indicator."", ""location"": ""discussion, p. 18"", ""reason"": ""Parent source inspection cannot establish that this is background only: the paper explicitly re-tests cross-cultural moderation with a changed adjustment measure. Measure differences alone do not rule out a conceptual replication. The two allowed Argon calls are exhausted; this proposed target remains unverified rather than being excluded on this quotation.""}","{""authors"": ""Diener, E., Tay, L., & Myers, D. G."", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""The religion paradox: If religion makes people happy, why are so many dropping out?"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Study 1 was a direct replication of previous cross-cultural research on the religiosity- adjustment relation. Yet, this study differed from previous research in three important ways. First, previous research operationalized psychological adjustment as life satisfaction (Stavrova et al., 2013), subjective well-being (Diener et al., 2011), depression (Leurent et al., 2013), or social self-esteem (Gebauer et al., 2012b). "", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Our results fully and firmly replicated and extended prior evidence for cross-cultural differences in religious adjustment benefits."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The reported moderation agrees with the prior positive moderation findings.""}"
