10.1037/pspp0000104,9c0e3d488066f983,3,,Spiritual and religious beliefs as risk factors for the onset of major depression: an international cohort study.,"Leurent, B., Nazareth, I., Bellon-Saameno, J., Geerlings, M-I., Maaroos, H., Saldivia, S., Svab, I., Torres-Gonzalez, F., Xavier, M., & King, M.",2013,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,"{""target_index"": 3, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""obvious"", ""verdict"": ""undeterminable"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""Yet, this study differed from previous research in three important ways. First, previous research operationalized psychological adjustment as life satisfaction (Stavrova et al., 2013), subjective well-being (Diener et al., 2011), depression (Leurent et al., 2013), or social self-esteem (Gebauer et al., 2012b). From an RASV perspective, however, global self-esteem is the most appropriate adjustment indicator."", ""location"": ""discussion, p. 18"", ""reason"": ""Parent source inspection cannot establish that this is background only: the paper explicitly re-tests cross-cultural moderation with a changed adjustment measure. Measure differences alone do not rule out a conceptual replication. The two allowed Argon calls are exhausted; this proposed target remains unverified rather than being excluded on this quotation.""}","{""authors"": ""Leurent, B., Nazareth, I., Bellon-Saameno, J., Geerlings, M-I., Maaroos, H., Saldivia, S., Svab, I., Torres-Gonzalez, F., Xavier, M., & King, M."", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": ""Spiritual and religious beliefs as risk factors for the onset of major depression: an international cohort study."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Study 1 was a direct replication of previous cross-cultural research on the religiosity- adjustment relation. Yet, this study differed from previous research in three important ways. First, previous research operationalized psychological adjustment as life satisfaction (Stavrova et al., 2013), subjective well-being (Diener et al., 2011), depression (Leurent et al., 2013), or social self-esteem (Gebauer et al., 2012b). "", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The cumulative results provide unequivocal support for RASV and for cross-cultural differences in the religiosity-adjustment relation."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The new moderation conflicts with the explicitly reported absence of moderation in this original; comparison spans introduction and discussion, so confidence is lower.""}"
