10.1177/2053168018822174,6070e18087845e69,2,,Risk orientations and policy frames.,Kam CD and Simas EN,2010,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Kam CD and Simas EN"", ""year"": ""2010"", ""title"": ""Risk orientations and policy frames."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Our third experiment replicates Kam and Simas (2010), who show that risk acceptance correlates with choosing the risky option in an Asian Disease-type experiment, but that the treatment effect of the mortality frame does not vary appreciably with risk acceptance."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""This finding was replicated in both MTurk and Lucid samples."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors report agreement with the original experimental finding.""}"
