10.1186/s13018-018-0769-2,f7079a3b8eb85bc0,4,10.1302/2046-3758.55.2000589,No association of the single nucleotide polymorphism rs8044769 in the fat mass and obesity-associated gene with knee osteoarthritis risk and body mass index: a population-based study in China,"Wang Y, Chu M, Rong J, Xing B, Zhu L, Zhao Y, et al.",2016,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Wang Y, Chu M, Rong J, Xing B, Zhu L, Zhao Y, et al."", ""year"": ""2016"", ""title"": ""No association of the single nucleotide polymorphism rs8044769 in the fat mass and obesity-associated gene with knee osteoarthritis risk and body mass index: a population-based study in China"", ""doi"": ""10.1302/2046-3758.55.2000589"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""A study on Chinese Han population denied this association, but the subject number of the Chinese study was a little bit small [16]. Until now, the association between FTO and OA remains debatable.Therefore, we evaluated the potential association of the FTO polymorphism (rs8044769) with OA in the Chinese Han population with more cases and controls."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Our results were consistent with a previous study in Chinese population and had enlarged studied subjects. We also conducted a meta-analysis together with the previous study in Chinese population to offer a solid evidence that rs8044769 of FTO was not associated with OA risk or BMI in Chinese population."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The explicitly motivated larger Chinese sample re-tests the earlier Chinese null and agrees. The new sample independently re-tests this finding; the accompanying pooled meta-analysis is not the sole basis.""}"
