st modest impacts on subsequent impulsive choice,\n\ncompared to relatively larger impacts of exposure to delayed\n\nreinforcement. This was true in the present experiment"", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The introduction identifies the set of prior immediate-reinforcement findings whose generality is tested; the discussion explicitly reports consistency with every named member of that set. Modest magnitude is not framed as failure.""}"
