10.1016/j.physbeh.2010.12.015,6ed3253ec5d2e142,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We have previously observed increased basal acoustic startle response (ASR) in Wistar rats exposed to stress or dexamethasone (DEX) in utero when tested during the light phase of the circadian rhythm, and decreased prepulse inhibition (PPI) in similar animals tested during the dark phase of the cycle."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We hereby replicated our earlier findings in a new strain and laboratory, thus strengthening the validity of our model regarding prenatal stress effects on ASR in female offspring."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit overall replication verdict. Original bibliographic identity and number of original papers cannot be resolved from abstract; unnamed target represents the earlier basal-startle finding, not an inferred reference.""}"
