that describing someone as a voter (noun) instead of one who votes (verb) increases turnout rates 11 to 14 points because the noun activates a person's social identity as a voter."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We find no evidence that this minor wording change increases turnout levels."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract states the original positive noun-versus-verb turnout finding and this replication finds no evidence of the increase.""}"
