10.1016/j.bbr.2024.115096,a23c52a8487df33f,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""A previous study with Virtual Reality (VR) and online motion-capture quantified this approach bias towards food and non-food cues in a controlled VR environment with hand movements. The aim of this study was to test the specificity of a manual approach bias for high-calorie food in grasp movements compared to low-calorie food and neutral objects of different complexity, namely, simple balls and geometrically more complex office tools."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The results confirm the presence of bottom-up advantages in motor-cognitive behaviour for high-calorie food in a non-clinical population."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract states the earlier approach bias and confirms the corresponding high-calorie approach advantage. Citation unavailable in abstract.""}"
10.1080/08870446.2013.841911,0299dc23292234ca,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,"{""corrected_value"": null, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""0299dc23292234ca"", ""location"": ""Abstract (line 4)"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""OBJECTIVE: The study's aim was to investigate psychological, behavioral and medical long-term outcomes of an existing self-management intervention targeting the development of proactive coping skills (e.g. goal setting and identifying barriers) in type 2 diabetes patients. The study aimed to replicate prior research showing the intervention's effectiveness, and to extend it by (a) adding booster sessions and (b) prolonging the period of follow-up measurement to capture long-term effects."", ""reason"": ""The supplied primary source text (0299dc23292234ca.txt) consists only of the title, author list, and abstract, and no prior adjudication or state file exists for this never-adjudicated work. In the abstract, Kroese et al. state that the study 'aimed to replicate prior research showing the intervention's effectiveness, and to extend it by (a) adding booster sessions and (b) prolonging the period of follow-up measurement to capture long-term effects' for an existing 5-step proactive-coping self-management intervention in type 2 diabetes patients. However, the abstract does not name or cite any specific original author, year, title, or DOI. Shipped row input_row_index 1833 (Thoolen; de Ridder; Bensing; Gorter; Rutten, 2007, 'Beyond Good Intentions: the development and evaluation of a proactive self-management course for patients recently diagnosed with Type 2 diabetes', 10.1093/her/cyl160, verified in bibliography_metadata.json) evaluates a proactive self-management course co-authored by senior author Denise de Ridder and is a plausible candidate for the retested intervention study. The precise unresolved question is whether the unnamed 'prior research' empirically retested in this paper is specifically Thoolen et al. (2007) (input_row_index 1833), a related report on the same trial/cohort, or a different original study, which cannot be settled from the abstract-only source without the full text and reference list."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0000_0299dc23292234ca"", ""target_index"": 0, ""verdict"": ""undeterminable""}","{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The study aimed to replicate prior research showing the intervention's effectiveness, and to extend it by (a) adding booster sessions and (b) prolonging the period of follow-up measurement to capture long-term effects."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The original intervention is effective, but the added value of the booster sessions is uncertain."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The conclusion supports the original intervention overall. Added booster sessions are an extension. The abstract does not identify the original citation; its number of original papers cannot be established.""}"
