10.1109/iccq60895.2024.10576941,a8a14f7870a16609,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This paper presents a conceptual replication of a previous experimental study that evaluated two practices associated with source code readability, namely, use of comments and method chaining."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Concerning perceived readability, our study found no significant differences between method chaining variants and between comment variants. The original study did find a significant difference for comments variants. In the case of comprehension, we found no significant differences between the method chaining variants but found a significant difference for an$a= 0.1\\%$among comments variants, both as opposed to the original study."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Perceived readability agrees for method chaining but disagrees for comments; comprehension results are explicitly opposed to the original. The abstract does not identify the original citation.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0313619,27ef689bc56b0705,1,10.1038/s41598-017-15339-z,Body size estimation in women with anorexia nervosa and healthy controls using 3D avatars,"Cornelissen K. K., McCarty K., Cornelissen P. L. & Tovée M. J.",2017,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Cornelissen K. K., McCarty K., Cornelissen P. L. & Tovée M. J."", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": ""Body size estimation in women with anorexia nervosa and healthy controls using 3D avatars"", ""doi"": ""10.1038/s41598-017-15339-z"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In summary, the current study serves both as a replication and extension of Cornelissen et al. [17,18]."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""When analysing the entire clinical group, their self-estimated BMI closely matched their actual BMI, evidenced by a regression slope close to one (see Fig 2), suggesting a relatively accurate perception of own body size across the actual BMI range. However, excluding the participants with a history of bulimia nervosa and repeating the analysis, yielded results more consistent with Cornelissen et al. [17,18], as illustrated in Fig 3. Specifically, the regression slope of estimated BMI on actual BMI had a slope > 1, with accurate estimation at low actual BMI, and systematically increasing overestimation as actual BMI increased."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors describe agreement on the group-by-BMI interaction and psychological contribution, but a full clinical-group slope near one rather than the originals’ accelerating overestimation. Excluding bulimia participants restores the original pattern. The stated replication of the key interaction concerns one finding, not an overall verdict overriding the described difference.""}"
10.1007/bf02298289,1d3010abd6bf7fd2,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,"{""corrected_value"": null, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""1d3010abd6bf7fd2"", ""location"": ""Abstract (line 23)"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""In this article, Salomon's model and the research in which the model was tested are discussed, and a replication study is presented. The study determines the internal structure of the Dutch versions of Salomon's instruments and tests some predictions following from the model. Unlike their American peers, Dutch children do not unconditionally perceive television as an easy medium."", ""reason"": ""No prior adjudication or state file exists for this work. The supplied primary source contains only the publisher landing-page abstract and reference list for Beentjes (1989). The abstract states that it presents a Dutch replication study determining the internal structure of Dutch versions of Salomon's instruments, testing predictions from Salomon's (1981) model, and comparing Dutch children's media perceptions to those of their American peers. However, the abstract does not cite which empirical study is replicated, and the reference list contains two distinct 1984 empirical articles on children's media perceptions and effort investment: Salomon (1984), 'Television is \""easy\"" and print is \""tough\"": The differential investment of mental effort in learning as a function of perceptions and attributions' (Journal of Educational Psychology, 74, 647-658), and Salomon & Leigh (1984), 'Predispositions about learning from print and television' (Journal of Communication, 34, 119-135), the latter of which is shipped row 1863 (DOI 10.1111/j.1460-2466.1984.tb02164.x). Without the article body, the evidence cannot resolve whether the retested target is already represented by shipped row 1863, is Salomon (1984), or includes both."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0009_1d3010abd6bf7fd2"", ""target_index"": 0, ""verdict"": ""undeterminable""}","{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In this article, Salomon's model and the research in which the model was tested are discussed, and a replication study is presented. The study determines the internal structure of the Dutch versions of Salomon's instruments and tests some predictions following from the model."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract contrasts Dutch and American media perceptions but does not identify which original empirical paper supplies the American result. Two 1984 reference entries fit the media-perception finding, so an outcome cannot be assigned to a uniquely identified target. The 1981 book is cited as the source of the model, not explicitly as the original empirical finding.""}"
10.17605/osf.io/82bwv,92e046b18547f955,1,,,"Riesel, Weinberg, Moran, & Hajcak",2013,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Riesel, Weinberg, Moran, & Hajcak"", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Therefore, we attempted this same analysis strategy and performed a median split based on ERN amplitude and re-assessed the correlation between ERN and EPS magnitude in this subgroup of participants (see Figure 4)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Consistent with the Riesel et al. (2013) study, we found a significant correlation between ERN and EPS in this subgroup of participants (r = -.63, p < .01)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Additional analysis explicitly re-tests the later published subgroup finding and reports agreement. The subsequent removal of an outlier is exploratory. Citation is inline only; title and DOI are absent.""}"
10.1016/j.appet.2013.12.020,98ff6e79db78401a,0,10.1037/0022-3514.92.2.325,Self-control relies on glucose as a limited energy source. Willpower is more than a metaphor.,"Gailliot, M. T., Baumeister, R. F., DeWall, C. N., Maner, J. K., Plant, E. A., Tice, D. M., et al.",2007,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Gailliot, M. T., Baumeister, R. F., DeWall, C. N., Maner, J. K., Plant, E. A., Tice, D. M., et al."", ""year"": ""2007"", ""title"": ""Self-control relies on glucose as a limited energy source. Willpower is more than a metaphor."", ""doi"": ""10.1037/0022-3514.92.2.325"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""8, 9"", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""The present study was designed to comply with the widespread call for replications by applying study protocols reported to results in substantial effects of sugar consumption (Gailliot et al., 2007; Wang & Dvorak, 2010) and sugar sensing (Hagger & Chatzisarantis, 2012; Molden et al., 2012) on ego depletion. The resulting observation that these procedures did not lead to the detection of the originally reported effects underscores the relevance of independent replications."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Two experimental designs involving highly reliable, prototypical self-control tasks and yielding more than sufﬁcient power failed to replicate the previously reported effects of glucose ingestion (Gailliot et al., 2007; Hagger et al., 2010) and glucose sensing (Hagger & Chatzisarantis, 2012; Molden et al., 2012)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly report failure to replicate this published glucose effect. Limitations are discussed, but their substantive overall judgment remains failure, rather than an inability to adjudicate.""}"
