10.1111/bjso.12371,90ac410fbfe5387b,1,10.1371/journal.pone.0088852,The impact of weather on women’s tendency to wear red or pink when at high risk for conception,"Tracy, J. L., & Beall, A. T.",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Tracy, J. L., & Beall, A. T."", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""The impact of weather on women’s tendency to wear red or pink when at high risk for conception"", ""doi"": ""10.1371/journal.pone.0088852"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Having found inconclusive evidence in Study 1 for an effect of conception risk on the likelihood of wearing red or pink on relatively cold days, in Study 2 (Analysis I) we used data from a large sample collected online between February 2015 and May 2015 to more closely replicate Beall and Tracy (2013) and Tracy and Beall (2014)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The studies we presented here, which incorporated conceptual replications, close replications, and extended replications of the original studies reporting that women are more likely to wear red or pink at peak fertility (Beall & Tracy, 2013; Tracy & Beall, 2014), failed to reliably confirm the conjecture that women advertise their ovulatory status by wearing red, even on relatively cold days."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors give an overall failed-to-confirm verdict explicitly covering both original papers and all conceptual, close, and extended attempts. This overall verdict governs despite isolated supportive comparisons.""}"
10.1167/18.10.139,8b38dc8bb390979b,0,,,Moran et al.,2017,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Moran et al."", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Moran et al. (2017, VSS) found that realistic miniature increased immersion relative to unrealistic miniatures, but memory was unaffected. However, the questions used to assess memory were very easy, raising the possibility of a ceiling effect. The current experiment was very similar to Moran et al. (2017)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""However, immersion results failed to replicate: immersion scores did not significantly differ across the three conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The title focuses on immersion and this effect explicitly failed. The prior memory null was also recovered; under the title-specific coding rule the central immersion finding is failed. The directly repeated study is Moran et al. (2017), not the earlier Baranowski and Hecht paper. No reference list is available to expand the citation.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0126363,5e91a20ae553fe8f,0,10.1038/ng.2383,Large-scale association analysis provides insights into the genetic architecture and pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes,"Morris AP, Voight BF, Teslovich TM, Ferreira T, Segrè AV, Steinthorsdottir V, et al.",2012,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Morris AP, Voight BF, Teslovich TM, Ferreira T, Segrè AV, Steinthorsdottir V, et al."", ""year"": ""2012"", ""title"": ""Large-scale association analysis provides insights into the genetic architecture and pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes"", ""doi"": ""10.1038/ng.2383"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We selected 10 autosomal SNPs identified by European GWAS in 2012, including, rs12571751 in ZMIZ1, rs10842994 near KLHDC5, rs2796441 near TLE1, rs459193 near ANKRD55, rs10401969 in CILP2, rs12970134 near MC4R, rs7202877 near BCAR1, rs11063069 near CCND2, rs8108269 near GIPR [16], and rs8090011 in LAMA1 [15]."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In this study, we examined the association of 7 SNPs, rs12571751 in ZMIZ1, rs10842994 near KLHDC5, rs2796441 near TLE1, rs459193 near ANKRD55, rs10401969 in CILP2, rs12970134 near MC4R, and rs7202877 near BCAR1, with susceptibility to type 2 diabetes in a Japanese population, and found that rs12571751 in ZMIZ1 was significantly associated with type 2 diabetes in the Japanese population. We also examined the effects of 3 additional SNP loci, rs11063069 near CCND2 and rs8108269 near GIPR, which were identified in sex-differentiated analyses [16], and rs8090011 in LAMA1, which was shown to be associated with non-obese type 2 diabetes in European GWAS [15], but we did not replicate the original association in the Japanese population (Tables 4 and 5, S3 Table)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.17605/osf.io/8wd2b,c20f9db39f03cdd4,0,,Do defaults save lives?,"Johnson, E. J., & Goldstein, D.",2003,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Johnson, E. J., & Goldstein, D."", ""year"": ""2003"", ""title"": ""Do defaults save lives?"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""Experiment 1"", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In two well-powered samples (N = 1920), we conducted a close replication of the default effect in Johnson and Goldstein (2003) and in Johnson, Bellman, and Lohse (2002)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We successfully replicated Johnson and Goldstein (2003)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Overall verdict confirms this target despite smaller effects; both samples contributed to Part 1.""}"
10.17605/osf.io/8wd2b,c20f9db39f03cdd4,2,,,Van Dalen and Henkens,2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Van Dalen and Henkens"", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We based our extension on Van Dalen and Henkens (2014) who found that organ donation rates were higher when the option was temporary and would have to be renewed than when the default option was to donate."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In the first extension, we predicted that people would be more inclined to become donors when consent to organ donation is temporary. We found no evidence that consent varied between the temporary and permanent conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Extension 1 explicitly retests this cited temporal-choice finding in Sample 1. The supplied cache lacks its reference entry; title and DOI cannot be copied.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0246058,58d96ab64c094730,1,,Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs.,"Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B.",2019,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly state replication of this original paper’s finding about the strongest unique ideological associations. This is an additional retested finding in the exploratory analyses.""}"
10.30707/etd2019.george.a,f5cd9ebc971eb837,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Our research replicates a previous study, which examined how Christians being led to believe God will either include or exclude them influenced well-being scores."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract confirms the exclusion hypothesis but also reports an absent moderation; it gives neither the original results nor an overall replication verdict. It therefore cannot settle agreement across the original findings.""}"
10.1891/jcop.2005.19.4.309,63030915d136ccf9,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Research to date suggests that the best treatment for many mental disorders is provided through the combination of medications and psychotherapy (e.g., Hollon, Thase, & Markowitz, 2002). However, the majority of studies supporting this point have been done utilizing highly restricted, controlled samples that may not accurately reflect the way mental illness is treated in the community. The present study attempted to replicate those findings in an outpatient community clinic."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results showed that clients who took medications fared no better than clients who did not. These preliminary findings suggest that the combination of medications and psychotherapy may not be as effective in the “real world” as prior studies have implied, and point to the need for further research utilizing community samples."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The original claim of superior outcomes with combined medication and psychotherapy was explicitly retested. Authors report no advantage for combined treatment and contrast that result with prior findings.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,1,,Positive recency in delayed free recall,"Tzeng, OJL",1973,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Tzeng, OJL"", ""year"": ""1973"", ""title"": ""Positive recency in delayed free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors reexamine the prior CDFR findings jointly, but say only that previous studies had mixed results. They do not identify Tzeng’s original negative-recency result separately, so its agreement with the present robust negative recency cannot be determined.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,2,,Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall,"Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB",1974,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB"", ""year"": ""1974"", ""title"": ""Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The prior CDFR studies are jointly described as yielding mixed results without assigning individual findings. Present negative recency is clear, but agreement with this specific original is not established in the supplied article.""}"
