10.31275/20211931,ba34c6d310f46998,2,,Two attempted retro-priming replications show theory-relevant anomalous connectivity.,"Jolij, J., & Bierman, D.",2019,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Jolij, J., & Bierman, D."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""Two attempted retro-priming replications show theory-relevant anomalous connectivity."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Experiment 2 is a conceptual replication of the work\nreported in Jolij and Bierman (2019)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""2) The second experiment in this study (Experiment 2), a concept\u0002ual replication of the work reported by Jolij and Bierman (2019), yielded\nmarginal evidence (p = .064) of anomalous connectivity—of the same\norder of magnitude as found in Jolij and Bierman."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.7287/peerj.preprints.3352v1,c75e48cfc0df56cd,0,10.1002/dev.20062,Handedness and specific language impairment: A study of 6-year-old twins,"Bishop, D. V. M.",2005,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Bishop, D. V. M."", ""year"": ""2005"", ""title"": ""Handedness and specific language impairment: A study of 6-year-old twins"", ""doi"": ""10.1002/dev.20062"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In an attempt to replicate the previously reported relationship between language disorder and a reduced tendency to reach across the midline (Bishop, 2005; E. L. Hill & Bishop, 1998), we also assessed whether the probability of reaching to the seven spatial positions in the QHP task differed between the DLD and TD groups."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In particular, our failure to replicate a between-groups difference in the probability of reaching across the midline with the right hand indicates that this may not be a marker of compromised neurodevelopment relevant to language disorder, as previously suggested (Bishop, 2005; E. L. Hill & Bishop, 1998)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The corresponding published association is tested in the new twin sample and is not supported.""}"
