10.7287/peerj.preprints.3352v1,c75e48cfc0df56cd,4,10.7717/peerj.507,No population bias to left-hemisphere language in 4-year-olds with language impairment,"Bishop, D. V. M., Holt, G., Whitehouse, A. J. O., & Groen, M.",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Bishop, D. V. M., Holt, G., Whitehouse, A. J. O., & Groen, M."", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""No population bias to left-hemisphere language in 4-year-olds with language impairment"", ""doi"": ""10.7717/peerj.507"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We aimed to replicate previous findings of an association between DLD and reduced laterality on a quantitative measure of hand preference (reaching across the midline) and on language laterality assessed using functional transcranial Doppler ultrasound."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""There was no difference between the DLD and TD groups on quantitative measures of handedness or language lateralisation, or on a categorical measure of consistency of left hemisphere dominance."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The corresponding published association is tested in the new twin sample and is not supported.""}"
10.7287/peerj.preprints.3352v1,c75e48cfc0df56cd,5,10.1002/brb3.56,Does cerebral lateralization develop? A study using functional transcranial Doppler ultrasound assessing lateralization for language production and visuospatial memory,"Groen, M., Whitehouse, A. J. O., Badcock, N. A., & Bishop, D. V.",2012,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Groen, M., Whitehouse, A. J. O., Badcock, N. A., & Bishop, D. V."", ""year"": ""2012"", ""title"": ""Does cerebral lateralization develop? A study using functional transcranial Doppler ultrasound assessing lateralization for language production and visuospatial memory"", ""doi"": ""10.1002/brb3.56"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""A subsidiary aim was to see whether we could replicate associations between language laterality and language tests found by Groen et al. (2012)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In the second step of analysis, we tested the relationship between language and laterality from the opposite direction, using language measures as predictors, aiming to replicate the effects reported by Groen et al. (2012). We computed Spearman's correlations between each language measure and the fTCD laterality index in the two replication samples. However, no uncorrected correlation replicated across samples, and no correlation within a sample survived a Holm-Bonferroni correction."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The corresponding published association is tested in the new twin sample and is not supported.""}"
10.1016/j.evolhumbehav.2018.02.008,76565e99cc31903c,1,,"Partner choice, relationship satisfaction, and oral contraception: The congruency hypothesis.","Roberts, S. C., Little, A. C., Burriss, R. P., Cobey, K. D., Klapilová, K., Havlíček, J., et al.",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Roberts, S. C., Little, A. C., Burriss, R. P., Cobey, K. D., Klapilová, K., Havlíček, J., et al."", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""Partner choice, relationship satisfaction, and oral contraception: The congruency hypothesis."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Despite using exactly the same measures as used in all previous studies except one (Russell et al., 2014) as well as additional, well-validated alternative measures, we were unable to confirm the results concerning sexual satisfaction reported by Roberts, Little, et al. (2014) and Russell et al. (2014), or the results concerning jealousy reported by Cobey et al. (2013)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Despite using exactly the same measures as used in all previous studies except one (Russell et al., 2014) as well as additional, well-validated alternative measures, we were unable to confirm the results concerning sexual satisfaction reported by Roberts, Little, et al. (2014) and Russell et al. (2014), or the results concerning jealousy reported by Cobey et al. (2013)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly report failure to confirm the central finding of each of these three original papers. The Russell test includes a conceptual test of the attractiveness moderator.""}"
