10.31234/osf.io/2avns,e8b55999ba4ce0d0,1,,Primed lexical decisions: Combined effects of the proportion of related prime-target pairs and the stimulus-onset asynchrony of prime and target.,"De Groot, A. M. B.",1984,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""De Groot, A. M. B."", ""year"": ""1984"", ""title"": ""Primed lexical decisions: Combined effects of the proportion of related prime-target pairs and the stimulus-onset asynchrony of prime and target."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We also attempted to replicate the well-established associative-priming effect using a visual lexical decision task (e.g., de Groot, 1984, 1987; Neely, 1967, 1977)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The fact that we were able to replicate the robust associative-priming effect demonstrates that our participants were sufficiently motivated and illustrates that if an effect exists, our Bayesian methodology enables one to find evidence in its favor."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors state the verdict for this target or the expressly named effect set.""}"
