10.1123/pes.2021-0082,5d3847715036d23b,1,10.1123/pes.2017-0240,The effect of maturation on performance during repeated sprints with self-selected versus standardized recovery intervals in youth footballers.,"Brownstein CG, Ball D, Micklewright D, Gibson NV.",2018,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Brownstein CG, Ball D, Micklewright D, Gibson NV."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""The effect of maturation on performance during repeated sprints with self-selected versus standardized recovery intervals in youth footballers."", ""doi"": ""10.1123/pes.2017-0240"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Replicating the studies of Gibson et al and Brownstein et al to assess performance, and physiological, and perceived variables during a repeated sprint protocol (RSP) with standardized versus self-selected recovery in youth soccer players."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In contrast to the original studies, the present replication study demonstrated that self-selected recovery periods during a RSP leads to better repeated sprint performance compared with standardized recovery periods in youth soccer players. The better repeated sprint performance with individual recovery durations in RSP2 was achieved with less physiological and perceived effort."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The conclusion explicitly contrasts the central performance result with the original studies as a set, covering both named targets.""}"
