10.3389/fnbeh.2020.00128,cc4b8b7716b048a4,1,10.1093/scan/nsv059,Emotion regulation ability varies in relation to intrinsic functional brain architecture,Uchida M. Biederman J. Gabrieli J. D. E. Micco J. de Los Angeles C. Brown A. .,2015,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Uchida M. Biederman J. Gabrieli J. D. E. Micco J. de Los Angeles C. Brown A. ."", ""year"": ""2015"", ""title"": ""Emotion regulation ability varies in relation to intrinsic functional brain architecture"", ""doi"": ""10.1093/scan/nsv059"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This investigation is inspired by the study of Uchida et al. ( 2015 ). Because there are important differences concerning the operationalization of the constructs and the experimental procedure between our study and the Uchida study (see Supplementary Table S24 ), the current investigation can be a conceptual replication at best."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Thus, we can only conclude that the findings of the original study could not conceptually be replicated, the results do not extend to a different reappraisal strategy nor arousal instead of affect outcomes."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.1016/j.cognition.2020.104521,aef3bffe9de93fbe,1,10.1016/j.cognition.2014.06.011,Improving arithmetic performance with number sense training: An investigation of underlying mechanism,"Park, J., & Brannon, E. M.",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Park, J., & Brannon, E. M."", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""Improving arithmetic performance with number sense training: An investigation of underlying mechanism"", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.cognition.2014.06.011"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""Experiment 1"", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3, 4"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Consequently, we attempted more precise replications of Park & Brannon, 2013, 2014 in Experiment 3 (approximate arithmetic training compared to numeral ordering training) and a preregistered replication in Experiment 4 (approximate arithmetic training compared to approximate number comparison training)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The original goal of the current study was to replicate the finding that non-symbolic approximate arithmetic training improves symbolic arithmetic fluency, and to build on this finding by probing the mechanism of the transfer effect. However, we were unable to replicate the original finding across four independent experiments."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Overall failure verdict applies to both explicitly re-tested Park and Brannon papers; the subsequent pooled analysis does not change it.""}"
