10.1186/1748-7161-8-s2-o2,69b1f592e08ce7cf,1,10.1097/01.brs.0000216603.91330.6f,Association of estrogen receptor gene polymorphisms with susceptibility to adolescent idiopathic scoliosis,Wu J Qiu Y Zhang L Sun Q Qiu X He Y,2006,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Wu J Qiu Y Zhang L Sun Q Qiu X He Y"", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""Association of estrogen receptor gene polymorphisms with susceptibility to adolescent idiopathic scoliosis"", ""doi"": ""10.1097/01.brs.0000216603.91330.6f"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""It has been suggested that XbaI single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) (A/G rs934099) in estrogen receptor 1 (ESR1) may be associated with curve severity in Japanese AIS patients[ 1 ] and with both curve severity and predisposition for AIS in Chinese patients[ 2 ]. However, replication studies have not confirmed these findings[ 3 ]. The role of the XbaI ESR1 polymorphism rs9340799 in AIS has never been described in Caucasian AIS patients."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""No association between ESR1 XbaI polymorphism and AIS was found in the Caucasian population. None of the previously reported associations with curve severity, progression or operation rate could be confirmed."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract tests the previously reported ESR1 XbaI associations in a new Caucasian sample and explicitly states that no association was found and none of the prior associations could be confirmed.""}"
10.3389/fnins.2019.00078,e22b91e77b92663e,0,10.1016/j.neuropsychologia.2015.12.030,Anodal-tDCS over the human right occipital cortex enhances the perception and memory of both faces and objects,"Barbieri, M., Negrini, M., Nitsche, M. A., and Rivolta, D.",2016,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Barbieri, M., Negrini, M., Nitsche, M. A., and Rivolta, D."", ""year"": ""2016"", ""title"": ""Anodal-tDCS over the human right occipital cortex enhances the perception and memory of both faces and objects"", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.neuropsychologia.2015.12.030"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Thus, in the current study we conducted two experiments where we sought to replicate recent findings (Romanska et al., 2015;Barbieri et al., 2016) reporting enhanced face perception following transcranial electrical stimulation techniques. The primary aim of Experiment 1 was to replicate enhancements in face perception following anodal tDCS compared to sham stimulation, which were observed with a medium effect size and group sample sizes of 16 (Barbieri et al., 2016). "", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In sum, the current results failed to replicate previous findings of enhanced face perception using anodal tDCS (Experiment 1) and high-frequency tRNS (Experiment 2) targeting the occipitotemporal cortex."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.1111/head.12807,d81a6602f268754c,1,10.1097/AJP.0000000000000075,Molecular analysis of cluster headache,"Zarrilli F, Tomaiuolo R, Ceglia C, et al.",2015,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Zarrilli F, Tomaiuolo R, Ceglia C, et al."", ""year"": ""2015"", ""title"": ""Molecular analysis of cluster headache"", ""doi"": ""10.1097/AJP.0000000000000075"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) rs1126671 located in exon 7 of the ADH4 gene was associated with an increased risk for CH in two Italian studies, whereas rs1800759 located in the promoter region of ADH4 could only be associated with CH in the smaller case–control study. Thus, we performed a replication study on the ADH4 SNPs rs1126671 and rs1800759 in a large, Swedish case–control cohort in order to further investigate the possible contribution of ADH4 to CH."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The data did not support an association of the ADH4 SNPs rs1126671 and rs1800759 with CH."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors report no association for either variant, contrary to the associations reported by both cited Italian studies.""}"
10.1145/3416465.3416468,73f5176676324828,0,,Measuring cognitive load in introductory CS: Adaptation of an instrument.,"Morrison, Briana B., Dorn, Brian, and Guzdial, Mark",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Morrison, Briana B., Dorn, Brian, and Guzdial, Mark"", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""Measuring cognitive load in introductory CS: Adaptation of an instrument."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""RQ1 Morrison et al. [49] report good discriminant validity and internal reliability for a programming-domain adaptation of Leppink's [33] CL questionnaire, which is based on the threecomponent Old CLT. Do these findings replicate with a different cohort and a different programming tutorial?"", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We found that the questions targeting each CL type aligned with the other questions targeting that type, which supports the claim that the questionnaire has internal reliability. Moreover, we confirm strong support for the questionnaire's discriminant validity-that is, the IL-targeting, EL-targeting, and GL-targeting items appear to be measuring three distinct constructs."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.31234/osf.io/8wa6v,b114e585deb8cd91,1,,Altruism and indirect reciprocity: The interaction of person and situation in prosocial behavior,"Simpson B, Willer R.",2008,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Simpson B, Willer R."", ""year"": ""2008"", ""title"": ""Altruism and indirect reciprocity: The interaction of person and situation in prosocial behavior"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Towards the latter goal, we sought to conduct a conceptual replication of Simpson and Willer (2008) [39] to investigate if SVO has different relationships with decisionmaking in public versus private conditions."", ""outcome"": ""uninformative"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Notably, this analysis was underpowered and we cannot draw definitive conclusions whether SVO relates to responses to observation."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly say the SVO analysis was underpowered and cannot adjudicate the response-to-observation finding, despite some same-direction descriptive results.""}"
10.1016/j.euroecorev.2015.05.006,6986d6215bbf814f,1,,"The willingness to pay–willingness to accept gap, the “Endowment Effect,” subject misconceptions, and experimental procedures for eliciting valuations: comment.","Isoni, Andrea, Loomes, Graham, Sugden, Robert",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Isoni, Andrea, Loomes, Graham, Sugden, Robert"", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""The willingness to pay–willingness to accept gap, the “Endowment Effect,” subject misconceptions, and experimental procedures for eliciting valuations: comment."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""While we replicate the experiments of PZ and ILS as closely as possible and use features of their setup to identify subject misconceptions, Bartling et al. (forthcoming) focus on the claim in Cason and Plott (2014) that misconceptions about the BDM can be falsely interpreted as support for theories of framing, such as reference-dependent preferences."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Thus, we are not able to replicate the results on the valuations of mugs by PZ and ILS."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit failure verdict for the central mug valuation finding. Agreement in training lottery tasks does not overturn the failure of the focal effect.""}"
10.1177/0022466912449652,292446349ef54f27,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,"{""corrected_value"": null, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""292446349ef54f27"", ""location"": ""Abstract (line 4)"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""This replication study focused on the effectiveness of two different intervention approaches, activity-based intervention and embedded direct instruction, on the acquisition, generalization, and maintenance of phonological awareness, a key area of emergent literacy, by preschool children with language delays. Five male preschool participants with language delay were treated with a modified alternating-treatments design."", ""reason"": ""No prior adjudication or state file exists for this work. The supplied primary source (292446349ef54f27.txt) contains only the article title, author list, and abstract from Crossref JATS metadata, with no full text, in-text citations, or reference list. While the abstract explicitly states that this is a replication study comparing activity-based intervention and embedded direct instruction in five preschool children with language delays, it does not name or cite the original study being replicated, leaving all bibliographic fields of the blind candidate empty. Consequently, the available source evidence cannot settle the unresolved question of which specific published study is empirically retested in the full text and whether that target is already represented by shipped row 2529 (Losardo & Bricker, 1994, 'Activity-based intervention and direct instruction: a comparison study', doi_o: NA) or is a distinct unshipped original work."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0018_292446349ef54f27"", ""target_index"": 0, ""verdict"": ""undeterminable""}","{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This replication study focused on the effectiveness of two different intervention approaches, activity-based intervention and embedded direct instruction, on the acquisition, generalization, and maintenance of phonological awareness, a key area of emergent literacy, by preschool children with language delays."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract reports new results but neither identifies the original paper nor states its findings, so agreement cannot be assessed.""}"
https://openalex.org/w96171599,85d1ad39a05d633c,1,10.1038/ng.664,A genome-wide association study for myopia and refractive error identifies a susceptibility locus at 15q25.,"Hysi PG, Young TL, Mackey DA, Andrew T, Fernandez-Medarde A, Solouki AM, Hewitt AW, Macgregor S, Vingerling JR, Li YJ, Ikram MK, Fai LY, Sham PC, Manyes L, Porteros A, Lopes MC, Carbonaro F, Fahy SJ, Martin NG, van Duijn CM, Spector TD, Rahi JS, Santos E, Klaver CC, Hammond CJ",2010,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Hysi PG, Young TL, Mackey DA, Andrew T, Fernandez-Medarde A, Solouki AM, Hewitt AW, Macgregor S, Vingerling JR, Li YJ, Ikram MK, Fai LY, Sham PC, Manyes L, Porteros A, Lopes MC, Carbonaro F, Fahy SJ, Martin NG, van Duijn CM, Spector TD, Rahi JS, Santos E, Klaver CC, Hammond CJ"", ""year"": ""2010"", ""title"": ""A genome-wide association study for myopia and refractive error identifies a susceptibility locus at 15q25."", ""doi"": ""10.1038/ng.664"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We used the Age-Related Eye Disease Study (AREDS) cohort to replicate published significant associations at two loci on chromosome 15 from two genome-wide association studies (GWASs)."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Although use of the same SNPs used in the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia study did not show any evidence of association with refractive error in this AREDS sample, other SNPs within the candidate regions demonstrated an association with refractive error. Significant evidence of association was found using the hyperopia categorical trait, with the most significant SNPs rs1357179 on 15q14 (p=1.69×10 −3 ) and rs7164400 on 15q25 (p=8.39×10 −4 ), which passed the replication thresholds."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors contrast non-replication of the original SNPs with regional replication for hyperopia at this locus.""}"
10.36948/ijfmr.2025.v07i06.61995,c2ce02faa87b6213,0,,,,2013,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This study conducted a direct replication of Dzulkifli and Mustafar (2013) in an Indian university population."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""This direct replication of Dzulkifli and Mustafar (2013) failed to detect significant effects of colour priming on memory span or sustained attention in a sample of 60 Indian university undergraduates. Warm colour (red) background did not enhance cognitive performance relative to cool colour (blue) or white control conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly report failure to detect the two predicted effects. Low power is discussed, but authors explicitly say their null findings are informative. Target citation is unresolved because the sole Dzulkifli/Mustafar entry is a review, not the empirical primary study attributed in the prose.""}"
https://openalex.org/w1703767599,adb4867dd3755f27,1,,,Rothermund & Wentura,2004,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Rothermund & Wentura"", ""year"": ""2004"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""However, the construct validity of this type of IAT has been called into question by recent findings showing that the IAT score implying in-group preference is rather driven by the salience asymmetry within each categorical dyad of the procedure than by evaluative associations between concepts (Rothermund & Wentura, 2001, 2004)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Consistent with our predictions, results showed that in both cases salience asymmetries reliably predict the IAT effect."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract identifies both earlier salience-asymmetry findings and reports the corresponding predicted relationship in both new experiments. Bibliographic titles and original study numbers are absent from the abstract.""}"
