10.1525/collabra.163080,7bdaa130567dec72,1,10.1177/1948550611418535,Can uniform color color aggression? Quasi-experimental evidence from professional ice hockey,"Webster, G. D., Urland, G. R., & Correll, J.",2012,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Webster, G. D., Urland, G. R., & Correll, J."", ""year"": ""2012"", ""title"": ""Can uniform color color aggression? Quasi-experimental evidence from professional ice hockey"", ""doi"": ""10.1177/1948550611418535"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""We now extend our investigation to the modern NHL while attempting to address deficiencies in past research which supported the black uniforms-heightened aggression connection."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Also, we failed to find support for reduced aggression when wearing white uniforms (Webster et al., 2012) as we conducted comparisons within teams across eight seasons while ensuring the overall aggression in the league remained consistent (thus avoiding a history threat)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Study III directly addresses the modern NHL black-uniform and white-uniform findings, discusses methodological deficiencies in Webster, and reports failure for the white effect as well as the nested black-uniform analysis.""}"
https://hdl.handle.net/20.500.14721/40318,71aff154dfbcab0e,1,10.1016/j.jad.2021.05.047,How long do mood induction procedure (MIP) primes really last? Implications for cognitive vulnerability research.,"Gillies, J. C. P., & Dozois, D. J. A.",2021,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Gillies, J. C. P., & Dozois, D. J. A."", ""year"": ""2021"", ""title"": ""How long do mood induction procedure (MIP) primes really last? Implications for cognitive vulnerability research."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.jad.2021.05.047"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""The two dissertation studies aimed to test the reproducibility of findings from the original study (Gillies, 2018; Gillies & Dozois, 2021) by conducting an exact replication and extending the study design to address the three additional questions listed above."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Statistical analyses of data from these studies revealed results that largely support findings from the original study. That is, the MIPs were often ineffective for a substantial percentage of participants and induced sadness diminished quickly, often within 6 min."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""fulltext"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The lay summary gives an overall supportive verdict across both studies. The thesis and subsequent article report the same original sample, but the thesis uniquely reports the latent growth analyses; both are explicitly retested.""}"
